This is a bug fix, so no discussion was opened. It builds on #832, which this branch includes; once that merges, this diff is the second commit only.

## Problem

#440 stopped accessible prompts looping when stdin reaches EOF, and noted that it would be better to bubble up an error that stops execution. Without that error, when input ends mid-form every remaining prompt takes its default without running its validator, and `Run` returns nil. A required field can come back empty with no error.

The fallback also hid a second bug. Pressing Enter on a field with a default runs the validator on the empty line rather than on the default, so a required field refuses its own default. Piped input only got past it because EOF then fell back to the default; at a terminal the user is asked again until they retype it.

## Before and after

**Input ends early.** A select, an input, and a required input, with one answer piped:

| | `printf '2\n' \| go run .` |
|---|---|
| main | `cuisine="Greek" meal="" name="" err=<nil>` |
| this PR | `cuisine="Greek" meal="" name="" err=user aborted: input "Meal": reading input: EOF` |

**Enter on a default.** A required input with the default `Ada`, answered
with Enter:

| | output for `printf '\n' \| go run .` |
|---|---|
| main | `Name name is required`, asks again, then EOF falls back: `name="Ada" err=<nil>` |
| this PR | accepted first time: `name="Ada" err=<nil>` |

